---
import InnerPageLayout from "../../layouts/InnerPageLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../../components/CtaBand.astro";
import MetaMeasurementConsent from "../../components/MetaMeasurementConsent.astro";
import { site } from "../../data/site";
import "../../styles/builders-lab.css";

const membershipDescription = "Builders Lab is a $7/month Skool membership for builders and operators developing inspectable, practical AI systems. George Johnson will be active in the group daily and will share his current projects.";
const george = {
  "@type": "Person",
  name: "George B. Johnson",
  url: `${site.url}/`,
};
const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Builders Lab by George Johnson",
  description: membershipDescription,
  url: `${site.url}/builders-lab/`,
  about: {
    "@type": "Thing",
    name: "Inspectable practical AI systems",
  },
  author: george,
  mainEntity: {
    "@type": "Service",
    name: "Builders Lab membership",
    description: membershipDescription,
    provider: george,
    offers: {
      "@type": "Offer",
      price: "7",
      priceCurrency: "USD",
      url: new URL(site.skoolUrl, site.url).href,
      priceSpecification: {
        "@type": "UnitPriceSpecification",
        price: "7",
        priceCurrency: "USD",
        billingDuration: "P1M",
      },
    },
  },
};
---

<InnerPageLayout
  title="Builders Lab by George Johnson | Practical AI Systems"
  description={membershipDescription}
  canonicalPath="/builders-lab/"
  eyebrow="Skool membership"
  heading="Builders Lab by George Johnson"
  lead="Builders Lab is a $7/month membership on Skool for builders and operators developing inspectable, practical AI systems. George Johnson will be active in the group daily and will share his current projects."
  currentPage="Builders Lab"
  {schema}
>
  <section class="page-section section-pad lab-intro" aria-labelledby="working-title">
    <div class="section-label"><span>01</span><span>The membership</span></div>
    <div class="editorial-split">
      <h2 id="working-title">Build alongside George.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Membership is $7/month on Skool. George Johnson will be active in the group daily and will share his current projects there.</p>
        <p>Start with one repeated piece of work you understand. Define its source, record what happens, keep human judgment visible, and test the output.</p>
        <p>The point is not to make an AI system look autonomous. The point is to make the work clear enough that another capable person can review the path, the decisions, and the evidence.</p>
        <a class="button button-dark" href={site.skoolUrl} data-skool-cta="working-standard">Join Builders Lab on Skool — $7/month <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <p class="destination-note">Opens the Builders Lab membership page on Skool, where you can review the offer and join.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="lab-system section-pad" aria-labelledby="system-title">
    <div class="section-label section-label-light"><span>02</span><span>An inspectable system</span></div>
    <div class="lab-system-heading">
      <h2 id="system-title">A practical AI system leaves a reviewable trail.</h2>
      <p>Tools can change. This path keeps the operating logic visible.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="system-path" aria-label="Source to test system path">
      <li><span>01</span><h3>Source</h3><p>Name the material, request, or event that begins the work.</p></li>
      <li><span>02</span><h3>Record</h3><p>Save the input, status, and output in a form another person can inspect.</p></li>
      <li><span>03</span><h3>Review</h3><p>Check the result against explicit rules, constraints, and examples.</p></li>
      <li><span>04</span><h3>Approved handoff</h3><p>Make the responsible person and the next authorized action clear.</p></li>
      <li><span>05</span><h3>Test</h3><p>Run a bounded case, keep the evidence, and decide what changes next.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section page-section-alt section-pad" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
    <div class="section-label"><span>03</span><span>Decision guide</span></div>
    <div class="lab-decision-heading">
      <h2 id="fit-title">Bring a real workflow, not a claim you cannot test.</h2>
      <p>Membership signup takes place on Skool. Use the current Skool description to decide whether the working standard matches how you want to build.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-table" role="table" aria-label="Builders Lab decision guide">
      <div class="decision-row decision-head" role="row">
        <span role="columnheader">A useful starting point</span>
        <span role="columnheader">Reconsider the fit if</span>
      </div>
      <div class="decision-row" role="row">
        <span role="cell">One repeated workflow with a clear user and inspectable output.</span>
        <span role="cell">You want an AI system to make every decision without review.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="decision-row" role="row">
        <span role="cell">A sanitized artifact, example, or test result you can discuss.</span>
        <span role="cell">The work cannot be described without exposing private or restricted material.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="decision-row" role="row">
        <span role="cell">A willingness to narrow the scope and document what fails.</span>
        <span role="cell">You need a promise about income, rankings, or system reliability.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section section-pad" aria-labelledby="example-title">
    <div class="section-label"><span>04</span><span>George’s current projects</span></div>
    <div class="example-split">
      <div>
        <p class="mono-kicker">Active in the group daily</p>
        <h2 id="example-title">George shares the projects he is currently building.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>George Johnson will be active in the Builders Lab Skool group daily and will share his current projects there.</p>
        <p>AtsKaleSEO is one supporting example of the working standard: source material and records stay separate from review, approval, and publishing handoffs.</p>
        <p>Builders Lab is broader than any one project. The shared question is whether a practical AI system can be inspected, tested, and improved by the people responsible for it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    eyebrow="Builders Lab"
    title="Join Builders Lab on Skool for $7/month."
    text="George Johnson will be active in the Skool group daily and will share his current projects. Continue to Skool to review the membership and join."
    href={site.skoolUrl}
    label="Join Builders Lab on Skool — $7/month"
    external
    trackingName="final-review"
  />

  <MetaMeasurementConsent />

  <script>
    import "../../scripts/builders-lab.js";
  </script>
</InnerPageLayout>
